# The addons a client shell carries: one repository per line, as addons.lock names it, `#` comments.
#
# Read by tools/shell_lock.sh, which the shell export (tools/server.in: shell_lock_begin, shell_left_out_addons) and
# tools/check_shell_addons.sh use. Only these go into a shell build and its addons.lock; every other addons.lock line
# is for servers only, and its addon reaches a player as a gs-cloud overlay pack (GSCloudAddonSet).
#
# OWNER RULE: no game addon here, ever. fc-weapons, zee-gs-weapons, zed-gs-weapons, natural-disasters and anything else one
# game brings stay out of the shell: baked in, fc-weapons took the web pck from 44 MB to 147 MB, and a shell that carries a
# game's addon pins every game to that build's copy. tools/check_shell_addons.sh fails when this list names anything but a
# gs-* addon, or when addons.lock names a gs-* addon this list does not (add it here when the shell should carry it).
gs-2d
gs-achievements
gs-audio
gs-auth
gs-bot
gs-bot-record
gs-browser
gs-chat
gs-cloud
gs-combat
gs-console
gs-core
gs-economy
gs-effects
gs-entity
gs-flashlight
gs-friends
gs-fx
gs-game
gs-input
gs-inventory
gs-leaderboard
gs-lighting
gs-loadout
gs-locale
gs-log
gs-map
gs-match
gs-matchmaking
gs-menu
gs-mobile
gs-moderation
gs-net
gs-npc
gs-npc-ai
gs-npc-ai-director
gs-objective
gs-party
gs-peer-to-peer
gs-physics
gs-platform
gs-player
gs-player-char
gs-player-class
gs-player-controller
gs-procedural-generation
gs-profile
gs-profiler
gs-props
gs-radio
gs-replay
gs-save
gs-server
gs-server-query
gs-server-security
gs-settings
gs-sim
gs-spawn
gs-spectate
gs-sql
gs-stats
gs-team
gs-timer
gs-trail
gs-ui
gs-user
gs-user-avatar
gs-vehicle
